// spec: DCL-010
//
// A different message from 0017: 'super' is legal syntax inside a class, and
// what is wrong is that this class has no parent.
//
// ⚠️ The method is named 'Attempt', not 'Try'.  'try' is a keyword [LEX-010]
// and keywords fold case [SRC-010], so 'Try' is the keyword and the parser
// answers 'Expect procedure name.' -- a different refusal from the one this
// case exists to pin.

class Lonely;
begin
    procedure Attempt ();
    begin
        super.Something ();
    end
end

Lonely ().Attempt ();
